As shown in Fig. 3.7, the col and row values also give the central pixel location of the patch of input pixels used for calculating the output pixel for the thread. The nested for-loops in Fig. 3.8 (lines 10-11) iterate through all the pixels in the patch. We assume that the program has a defined constant BLUR_SIZE The value of BLUR_SIZE is set such that BLUR_SIZE gives the number of pixels on each side (radius) of the patch and 2*BLUR_SIZE+1 gives the total number of pixels across one dimension of the patch. For example, for a $3 \times3$ patch, BLUR_SIZE is set to 1, whereas for a $7 \times7$ patch, BLUR_SIZE is set to 3. The outer loop iterates through the rows of the patch. For each row, the inner loop iterates through the columns of the patch.

