We now turn our attention to the work done by each thread. Recall that $\mathrm{P_{row,col}}$ is calculated as the inner product of the rowth row of M and the colth column of N. In Fig. 3.11 we use a for-loop to perform this inner product operation. Before we enter the loop, we initialize a local variable Pvalue to 0 (line 06). Each iteration of the loop accesses an element from the rowth row of M and an element from the colth column of N, multiplies the two elements together, and accumulates the product into Pvalue (line 08).

